"text": "They would pour heavy cream into the baton, then shove a cork in the end. Each student would grab one, sprint 100 meters, and violently hand it to the next kid. You see, every stride shakes the cream, slamming fat molecules together as the contents begin to clump. The problem is this takes almost 30 minutes, so a normal relay becomes 80 sprints. And if someone drops the baton, the corks shoot out, and your team gets ejected for buttering lane three. Eventually, the runners collapse at the finish line, the judges crack open the batons, scoop out whatever survived, spread it on toast, and the tastiest breakfast wins.",
